        {
          "name": "pastepile_forget",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:95851f3170c25f4c60fb2a63977c9065bb440807d6b9bbf16d9ac016bcae1c1c",
          "description": "Permanently delete a paste from Pastepile. Use this when the user asks you to forget, remove, or delete something you saved earlier. With an API key configured you can delete any paste that was saved with that key, WITHOUT the one-time edit_key, which is what makes saved memory reversible across sessions. A paste saved with no key (or by someone else) needs its edit_key passed explicitly. Deletion is immediate and permanent: there is no undo and no trash. Confirm with the user before forgetting anything they did not just ask you to forget.",
